      "text": "# Torqvoice Workshop Management System — Stakeholder Analysis\n\n## Stakeholder Matrix\n\n| # | Stakeholder Role | Primary Interests | Influence | Impact if Needs Not Met |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **INTERNAL STAKEHOLDERS** |\n| 1 | **Workshop Owner / Manager** | Business profitability, revenue growth, multi-location management, accurate financial reporting, operational efficiency | **HIGH** | Loss of business oversight; inability to scale; poor financial decision-making; competitive disadvantage in market; potential business failure |\n| 2 | **Service Technician** | Quick job assignment, clear work order status, labor tracking, parts availability, performance metrics visibility | **HIGH** | Inefficient workflow; frustration leading to poor work quality; staff turnover; increased errors and rework; delayed customer service |\n| 3 | **Inventory/Parts Manager** | Stock level tracking, low-stock alerts, supplier ordering, parts cost management, historical usage patterns | **MEDIUM-HIGH** | Stock-outs causing service delays; excess inventory tying up capital; lost sales due to unavailable parts; supplier relationship breakdown; inflated costs |\n| 4 | **Administrative / Office Staff** | Customer data management, appointment scheduling, quote generation, invoice creation & sending, communication history | **HIGH** | Operational chaos; customer service failures; administrative burden; manual errors; missed invoicing; customer complaints; data loss |\n| 5 | **Bookkeeper / Accountant** | Financial accuracy, payment tracking (paid/unpaid/partial), tax-compliant reporting, audit trails, invoice reconciliation | **MEDIUM-HIGH** | Accounting errors; compliance violations; tax penalties; audit failures; delayed financial statements; inability to reconcile accounts |\n| 6 | **Service Advisor / Customer Service** | Customer communication, service history retrieval, quote sharing, status update notifications, problem resolution | **MEDIUM** | Poor customer satisfaction; miscommunication; complaints; lost repeat business; negative reputation; difficulty upselling services |\n| 7 | **Workshop IT / System Administrator** | System reliability, data security, backups, user access control, performance, system updates | **MEDIUM** | Data breaches; system downtime; lost customer/financial data; security incidents; compliance violations; business interruption |\n| **EXTERNAL STAKEHOLDERS** |\n| 8 | **Car Owner / Customer** | Transparent pricing, clear work status, easy invoice access, communication via preferred channels (email/SMS), public portal visibility | **HIGH** | Frustration; lost trust; negative online reviews; churn to competitor; word-of-mouth damage; reduced lifetime value; legal disputes |\n| 9 | **Auto Parts Supplier** | Timely order placement, accurate order quantities, payment on time, inventory visibility, supplier performance tracking | **MEDIUM** | Relationship strain; payment disputes; supply delays; reduced service level; potential account cancellation; loss of business opportunities |\n| 10 | **Payment Processor (Stripe)** | Correct transaction data, secure payment handling, accurate reconciliation, timely settlement | **MEDIUM** | Payment processing failures; chargebacks; account suspension; revenue loss; settlement delays; PCI compliance violations |\n| 11 | **Email / SMS Service Provider** | Reliable message delivery, correct recipient data, proper authentication, acceptable sending volumes | **LOW-MEDIUM** | Delivery failures; message bounces; poor customer communication; rate limiting; service blacklisting; account throttling |\n| 12 | **Insurance Company** | Accurate service records, clear documentation of work performed, labor hours, parts used for warranty claims | **LOW-MEDIUM** | Claim disputes; insufficient documentation; warranty claim denial; customer disputes; potential litigation; reputational damage |\n| 13 | **Government / Tax Authority** | Accurate financial records, sales tax collection & remittance, labor documentation, audit readiness, regulatory compliance | **MEDIUM** | Tax audit failures; penalties & interest charges; legal prosecution; business license suspension; reputational damage; fines |\n| 14 | **Banks / Financial Institutions** | Financial reporting accuracy, credit history, cash flow visibility, loan repayment history | **LOW** | Loan denial; unfavorable terms; higher interest rates; credit line restrictions; refinancing difficulties; cash flow problems |\n| 15 | **Competitors / Market** | N/A (external market force) | **INDIRECT** | Loss of market share; competitive disadvantage; inability to attract customers; pricing pressure; reduced market position; business decline |\n| 16 | **IT Support Vendor / Development Team** | System stability, feature requests, bug reports, performance monitoring, security patches | **MEDIUM** | Unresolved bugs; security vulnerabilities; poor system performance; delayed feature delivery; vendor relationship issues; customer support burden |\n| 17 | **End Users / Indirect Customers** (e.g., family members accessing shared customer portal) | Easy-to-use customer portal, mobile accessibility, transparent status updates, privacy | **LOW** | Poor user experience; portal avoidance; customer dissatisfaction; support tickets; negative feedback on usability |\n| 18 | **Cloud Hosting Provider** (if applicable) | System performance, uptime, security, data backup, disaster recovery | **MEDIUM** | System downtime; data loss; slow performance; security breaches; recovery failures; customer impact; SLA violations |\n| 19 | **Industry Associations / Certification Bodies** | Compliance with industry standards, data protection, quality metrics, best practices | **LOW-MEDIUM** | Non-compliance; loss of certifications; industry standards violations; reputation damage; market restrictions |\n| 20 | **Investors / Stakeholders** (if applicable) | ROI, user growth, revenue metrics, system scalability, competitive positioning | **MEDIUM-HIGH** | Poor investment returns; funding withdrawal; business valuation decline; inability to raise capital; strategic pivot required; exit pressure |\n\n---\n\n## Key Insights\n\n### Highest-Influence Stakeholders\n1. **Workshop Owner** — Controls business strategy and resource allocation\n2. **Technicians** — Day-to-day system users; impact on productivity and quality\n3. **Administrative Staff** — Critical gatekeepers of customer communication and data\n4. **Customers** — Revenue source; brand reputation risk\n\n### High-Impact External Relationships\n- **Customers** — Dissatisfaction can be amplified through reviews and word-of-mouth\n- **Payment Processor (Stripe)** — Account suspension would halt all revenue collection\n- **Suppliers** — Service disruptions affect ability to complete work\n- **Tax Authorities** — Non-compliance carries legal and financial penalties\n\n### Dependencies & Risk Areas\n- **Data Integrity** — Critical for accounting, compliance, customer trust\n- **System Uptime** — Any outage directly impacts revenue and customer service\n- **Communication Features** — Email/SMS failures damage customer relationships\n- **Financial Tracking** — Errors propagate to tax, accounting, and investor confidence\n- **Inventory Accuracy** — Affects service delivery and supplier relationships\n\n---\n\n## Engagement Strategy Recommendations\n\n| Stakeholder Category | Recommended Engagement | Frequency |\n|---|---|---|\n| **High-Influence, High-Impact** | Executive steering, direct communication, feedback loops | Monthly+ |\n| **High-Influence, Medium-Impact** | Regular feature requests, usability testing, training | Quarterly |\n| **Medium-Influence, High-Impact** | Operational support, process optimization, compliance updates | Quarterly |\n| **Low-Influence** | Standard support, documentation, self-service resources | As-needed |\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
