      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "# Torqvoice Workshop System Stakeholders\n\n| Name / role | Primary interest in the system | Influence | Impact if needs are not met |\n|---|---|---:|---|\n| Workshop owner / business owner | Run a profitable workshop, monitor revenue, control operations, manage staff, protect customer data, and configure company branding. | High | Poor adoption, lost revenue visibility, weak governance, and reduced confidence in the platform. |\n| Workshop manager / admin | Coordinate daily work, manage customers, vehicles, work orders, quotes, invoices, payments, inventory, and reports. | High | Operational delays, duplicate work, inaccurate records, and missed customer commitments. |\n| Service advisor | Create customer-facing quotes, explain service work, update statuses, send invoices, and communicate through email, SMS, or Telegram. | High | Customers receive unclear or late information, quote approvals slow down, and service handovers become error-prone. |\n| Technician | View assigned jobs, update work order progress, record inspections, findings, labor, parts, notes, and attachments. | High | Work quality and traceability suffer, jobs are delayed, and billing may miss labor or parts. |\n| Parts / inventory coordinator | Maintain part stock, supplier information, low-stock alerts, markup, and parts used on work orders. | Medium | Stockouts, over-ordering, incorrect margins, and delayed repairs. |\n| Billing / finance user | Track invoices, payment status, partial payments, recurring invoices, taxes, and payment provider reconciliation. | High | Revenue leakage, incorrect financial records, customer disputes, and weak cash-flow control. |\n| Reporting / business analyst user | Use revenue, service, customer, and inventory reports to understand performance and export data. | Medium | Management decisions rely on incomplete or stale information. |\n| Organization owner / team administrator | Manage organizations, invitations, roles, permissions, subscriptions, and feature access. | High | Unauthorized access, blocked users, poor tenant setup, and compliance risk. |\n| Super admin / platform operator | Administer system-wide users, organizations, settings, subscriptions, licenses, and support operations. | High | Platform support becomes slow, tenant issues escalate, and misconfiguration affects many workshops. |\n| Car owner / workshop customer | Request service, view vehicle history, review quotes, approve or reject quote items, view invoices, pay online, and receive status updates. | Medium | Lower trust, delayed approvals, payment friction, and increased phone/email workload for the workshop. |\n| Fleet customer / business customer | Track multiple vehicles, service history, invoices, and repeat service needs across a fleet. | Medium | Fleet downtime increases and the workshop may lose recurring commercial business. |\n| Parts supplier | Receive clear part requirements and support timely fulfillment for service work. | Low | Part delays affect repair completion and customer satisfaction. |\n| Payment provider | Process checkout, payment confirmation, refunds or status verification through integrations such as Stripe, PayPal, or Vipps. | Medium | Online payments fail or cannot be reconciled, increasing manual payment handling. |\n| Email provider | Deliver quotes, invoices, reports, password flows, and customer notifications through SMTP or providers such as Resend, Postmark, Mailgun, SendGrid, or SES. | Medium | Customers miss important documents and account or notification flows become unreliable. |\n| SMS / messaging provider | Deliver customer messages and inbound updates through Twilio, Vonage, Telnyx, or Telegram. | Medium | Status updates and customer conversations become fragmented or unavailable. |\n| AI provider | Support AI-assisted descriptions, service history summaries, common issue suggestions, and image-based part analysis when enabled. | Low | AI-assisted productivity features are unavailable, but core workshop operations can continue. |\n| External webhook consumer / integration owner | Receive signed event notifications for customers, vehicles, services, quotes, payments, inspections, inventory, and findings. | Medium | Downstream systems become stale and manual synchronization is required. |\n| Hosting / IT administrator | Deploy, back up, secure, monitor, and upgrade the self-hosted Docker app, PostgreSQL database, and uploads volume. | High | Data loss, downtime, security exposure, and failed upgrades. |\n| Regulator / auditor | Expect accurate records, access control, audit trails, tax handling, and appropriate protection of customer and vehicle data. | Medium | Compliance findings, legal exposure, and loss of customer trust. |\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "# Torqvoice Workshop System Stakeholders\n\n| Name / role | Primary interest in the system | Influence | Impact if needs are not met |\n|---|---|---:|---|\n| Workshop owner / business owner | Run a profitable workshop, monitor revenue, control operations, manage staff, protect customer data, and configure company branding. | High | Poor adoption, lost revenue visibility, weak governance, and reduced confidence in the platform. |\n| Workshop manager / admin | Coordinate daily work, manage customers, vehicles, work orders, quotes, invoices, payments, inventory, and reports. | High | Operational delays, duplicate work, inaccurate records, and missed customer commitments. |\n| Service advisor | Create customer-facing quotes, explain service work, update statuses, send invoices, and communicate through email, SMS, or Telegram. | High | Customers receive unclear or late information, quote approvals slow down, and service handovers become error-prone. |\n| Technician | View assigned jobs, update work order progress, record inspections, findings, labor, parts, notes, and attachments. | High | Work quality and traceability suffer, jobs are delayed, and billing may miss labor or parts. |\n| Parts / inventory coordinator | Maintain part stock, supplier information, low-stock alerts, markup, and parts used on work orders. | Medium | Stockouts, over-ordering, incorrect margins, and delayed repairs. |\n| Billing / finance user | Track invoices, payment status, partial payments, recurring invoices, taxes, and payment provider reconciliation. | High | Revenue leakage, incorrect financial records, customer disputes, and weak cash-flow control. |\n| Reporting / business analyst user | Use revenue, service, customer, and inventory reports to understand performance and export data. | Medium | Management decisions rely on incomplete or stale information. |\n| Organization owner / team administrator | Manage organizations, invitations, roles, permissions, subscriptions, and feature access. | High | Unauthorized access, blocked users, poor tenant setup, and compliance risk. |\n| Super admin / platform operator | Administer system-wide users, organizations, settings, subscriptions, licenses, and support operations. | High | Platform support becomes slow, tenant issues escalate, and misconfiguration affects many workshops. |\n| Car owner / workshop customer | Request service, view vehicle history, review quotes, approve or reject quote items, view invoices, pay online, and receive status updates. | Medium | Lower trust, delayed approvals, payment friction, and increased phone/email workload for the workshop. |\n| Fleet customer / business customer | Track multiple vehicles, service history, invoices, and repeat service needs across a fleet. | Medium | Fleet downtime increases and the workshop may lose recurring commercial business. |\n| Parts supplier | Receive clear part requirements and support timely fulfillment for service work. | Low | Part delays affect repair completion and customer satisfaction. |\n| Payment provider | Process checkout, payment confirmation, refunds or status verification through integrations such as Stripe, PayPal, or Vipps. | Medium | Online payments fail or cannot be reconciled, increasing manual payment handling. |\n| Email provider | Deliver quotes, invoices, reports, password flows, and customer notifications through SMTP or providers such as Resend, Postmark, Mailgun, SendGrid, or SES. | Medium | Customers miss important documents and account or notification flows become unreliable. |\n| SMS / messaging provider | Deliver customer messages and inbound updates through Twilio, Vonage, Telnyx, or Telegram. | Medium | Status updates and customer conversations become fragmented or unavailable. |\n| AI provider | Support AI-assisted descriptions, service history summaries, common issue suggestions, and image-based part analysis when enabled. | Low | AI-assisted productivity features are unavailable, but core workshop operations can continue. |\n| External webhook consumer / integration owner | Receive signed event notifications for customers, vehicles, services, quotes, payments, inspections, inventory, and findings. | Medium | Downstream systems become stale and manual synchronization is required. |\n| Hosting / IT administrator | Deploy, back up, secure, monitor, and upgrade the self-hosted Docker app, PostgreSQL database, and uploads volume. | High | Data loss, downtime, security exposure, and failed upgrades. |\n| Regulator / auditor | Expect accurate records, access control, audit trails, tax handling, and appropriate protection of customer and vehicle data. | Medium | Compliance findings, legal exposure, and loss of customer trust. |\n",
